--[[
	Anomaly Coop - tents and sleeping bags on a co-op machine: the adapter of the stock item_tent
	(gamedata\scripts\coop_tent_guard.script). F3 hotfix (a client got a message), rewritten by F3 task 13 (a client asks the
	host). Research: docs\research\2026-10-22-f3-saves-sleep-recon.md, B.3 and Z2 / Z6 / Z7 / Z8.
	What the player sees and the claims themselves: coop_checkpoints.script (request, tips).

	F3a task 7 (docs/plans/2026-10-24-f3a-split-levels.md 1.2): the roles of the process, not "host / client". The host's
	process is the world server AND a player - the host player is a client of his own world server over the internal
	channel. So everything below that says "a client" is now "a PLAYER" (coop.is_player(): a remote client and the host
	player alike), and "the host" is "the WORLD SERVER" (coop.is_world_server()). The host player's tent goes up the way a
	client's does (a claim; the engine puts it up for peer 0); the stock no longer puts it up and no report of a stock tent
	exists any more (coop_checkpoints.report_placed is gone with this change: the host would have claimed twice). A build
	without the role functions falls back to the old pair.

	Why. A client cannot create a world object: the engine returns nil for alife_create without a parent (the host does not
	take such a request). The stock item_tent then reads se_obj.id of that nil:
	  - itm_tent_func runs as a level.add_call functor (no pcall): a Lua error there is FATAL in a release build;
	  - the sleeping bag branch of the local actor_on_item_use fails the same way, the item is lost;
	  - packing a tent / bag up releases the host's object, which a client may not do: the item is handed out twice.
	And the stock func_use_tent / func_use_bag free the used item themselves (CreateTimeEvent 0) about 4 s BEFORE a tent would
	be put up. So on a client the stock functions never run.

	What on a co-op CLIENT (Ruling F3-6, F3 T7 round 1). The host puts the tent up and takes the item from the client's
	inventory itself (no item: the host refuses, "no_item"), so the client does not touch the item at all, whatever the
	use does:
	  tent / sleeping bag    coop_checkpoints.request("tent" | "sleepbag"): after the put-up animation (4 s with the video
	                         option, as stock; a sleeping bag at once) coop.checkpoint.claim_tent(x, y, z, what) with the spot
	                         3 m ahead (a bag: under the player). The item stays; the host's answer is a camp on the tent, a
	                         refusal, or nothing (the wait ends by itself);
	  itm_tent_bag, compression_bag, using any tent of mine (Ruling F3-11)
	                         "pack": the host gives back the item it took, for the tent at the spot of the claim. No bag is
	                         handed out to a client. A tent is mine when it is or was my camp (the client remembers them) or
	                         carries my owner key on its custom data. A sleeping bag is used to sleep (stock): it is packed up by a
	                         compression bag or by coop_checkpoints.pack_nearby() (a button of the sleep window, F3 T14).
	Entry points (assigned into the item_tent module table at load time, so everything that looks them up later by name finds
	the wrapper, including the local actor_on_item_use of the stock file, which calls start_timer and use_compression_bag
	through the module table):
	  func_use_tent, func_use_bag   use1_action_functor of the items (stock itm_tent, GAMMA itm_sleepbag too): not eaten by
	                                the engine, the stock function would free the item - it is not called on a client;
	  start_timer, use_compression_bag, itm_tent_func, itm_tent_bag_func   the stock timer and pack-up functions: nothing on
	                                a client (a mod may call them); with use_placeable = false the stock runs as it is;
	  get_nearby_tent               in a session: looks at every online tent of the list, not at the first one (review I-2). The
	                                clients' tents are in the list on the host, and the stock answers by the first online
	                                tent whichever it is, so the host would not find his own. The host's own first (his claimed
	                                tents, then unclaimed ones, then the clients'), a client's own (the camps he remembers,
	                                even when the host's snapshot of the list lacks them) first; nil for no tent online, false
	                                for none in reach, as stock;
	  on_game_start                 after the stock one has registered its local use callback, that callback is replaced:
	                                on a client it turns the four sections of the stock into claims, and everything else goes
	                                on to the stock callback unchanged.
	The engine eats an item used from the inventory (CInventory::Eat deletes it when remove_after_use is true (default) and
	max_uses is 1): stock Anomaly eats itm_sleepbag; GAMMA does not (the action functor). When the engine did eat it, the
	client creates it again first (alife_create_item with the actor as parent, which the host accepts) and claims a moment
	later; itm_tent_bag and compression_bag (remove_after_use = false) stay and are never given back.
	With use_placeable = false in itms_manager.ltx the stock uses the item directly (no object is put up): left to the stock.

	What on the WORLD SERVER. A tent the engine put up for a player (callback coop_tent_placed(tent, character), the host
	player's too) is added to item_tent's lists (CHECKPOINTS_DEATH 10.2); the callback queue is lossy, so the first update of
	a world adds, from the objects of the world, every tent and sleeping bag coop.checkpoint.tent_owner(id) names. A world
	server that is no player (none yet) leaves the stock alone.

	Single player and an exe without co-op: every wrapper calls the stock function with the same arguments.
	Loaded by axr_main like any script that has on_game_start; nothing is added to coop_main or the domain tables (the name
	falls under coop_* = view; the callbacks are view callbacks, pcall-protected on a client like the stock one).
--]]

local api = rawget(_G, "coop") -- engine namespace (nil on an exe without co-op)

local USE_CALLBACK = "actor_on_item_use"
local ANIMATION_MS = 4000 -- stock: the put-up animation with the video option "video/player/animations"
local GIVE_BACK_MS = 1500 -- the item the engine ate is created again; the claim waits for it to reach the host

stats = { claims = 0, given_back = 0, return_failed = 0, registered = 0, reconciled = 0 }

local function log(fmt, ...)
	local ok, line = pcall(string.format, fmt, ...)
	printf("[coop-tent-guard] %s", ok and line or tostring(fmt))
end

local function checkpoints()
	return rawget(_G, "coop_checkpoints") or coop_checkpoints
end

-- Roles are asked at every call (the role is not known when the script loads).
local function in_session()
	if not api then return false end
	local ok, active = pcall(api.is_active)
	return ok and active == true
end

-- F3a task 7: a player asks (a remote client, the host player); the world server keeps the stock lists. A build without the
-- role functions has the old pair.
local function is_player()
	if not in_session() then return false end
	local f = type(api.is_player) == "function" and api.is_player or api.is_client
	local ok, yes = pcall(f)
	return ok and yes == true
end

local function is_world_server()
	if not in_session() then return false end
	local f = type(api.is_world_server) == "function" and api.is_world_server or api.is_host
	local ok, yes = pcall(f)
	return ok and yes == true
end

local function section_of(obj)
	if obj == nil then return nil end
	local ok, sec = pcall(function() return obj:section() end)
	return ok and type(sec) == "string" and sec or nil
end

local function upvalue(f, name)
	if type(f) ~= "function" then return nil end
	for i = 1, 255 do
		local n, v = debug.getupvalue(f, i)
		if n == nil then return nil end
		if n == name then return v end
	end
	return nil
end

local function animation_ms()
	local ok, on = pcall(function() return ui_options.get("video/player/animations") end)
	return (ok and on) and ANIMATION_MS or 0
end

local function play_fx()
	pcall(function() actor_effects.play_item_fx("itm_sleepbag") end)
end

-- Did the engine take the item for this use? CInventory::Eat deletes it only when remove_after_use is true (default) and
-- no use is left (max_uses, default 1). An unreadable section counts as "not taken": no give-back, no duplicate.
local function eaten_for_good(section)
	local ok, r = pcall(function()
		-- no default argument for r_float_ex: the non-memoizing variant of _g.script ignores it and returns nil
		return ini_sys:r_bool_ex(section, "remove_after_use", true) and (ini_sys:r_float_ex(section, "max_uses") or 1) <= 1
	end)
	return ok and r == true
end

-- Put one back in the inventory (the parent is the actor, so the client's request is forwarded and accepted).
local function give_back(section)
	local actor = db.actor
	if not (section and actor and eaten_for_good(section)) then return false end
	local ok, err = pcall(alife_create_item, section, actor)
	if ok then
		stats.given_back = stats.given_back + 1
	else
		stats.return_failed = stats.return_failed + 1
		log("! could not return %s: %s", section, tostring(err))
	end
	return ok
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The stock module's lists
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
local function stock_module()
	return rawget(_G, "item_tent")
end

-- item_tent.get_spawned_tents() / get_spawned_sleepbags(): { [object id] = true }
local function spawned(getter)
	local m = stock_module()
	local f = m and m[getter]
	if type(f) ~= "function" then return nil end
	local ok, t = pcall(f)
	return ok and type(t) == "table" and t or nil
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- A player uses an item: the item stays, the world server is asked
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
local function client_item(c, obj, orig, ...)
	local kind = c.item_kind(section_of(obj))
	if kind == nil then
		-- no tent of ours: the stock function would free the item, so it is not called either
		c.tell("unsupported", true)
		return
	end
	if kind ~= "pack" and not c.placeable(kind) then return orig(obj, ...) end -- the ltx says "do not put up": stock
	if kind == "tent" then
		if c.request("tent", animation_ms()) then play_fx() end
	else
		c.request(kind, 0)
	end
	stats.claims = stats.claims + 1
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The use callback of the stock file
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
local stock_use = nil -- the file local actor_on_item_use of item_tent (an upvalue of func_use_tent / func_use_bag)
local use_guard = nil -- what replaces it in the callback list

-- The branch of the stock callback that places a ph_sleepbag: SleepBagEnable and SleepBagSections[sec] and SleepBagPlaceable
-- (the stock file locals, read as upvalues at call time).
local function sleepbag_branch(sec)
	local sections = upvalue(stock_use, "SleepBagSections")
	return upvalue(stock_use, "SleepBagEnable") and upvalue(stock_use, "SleepBagPlaceable")
		and type(sections) == "table" and sections[sec] ~= nil
end

local function swap_use_callback()
	local old = stock_use
	if type(old) ~= "function" then return end
	local cm = rawget(_G, "coop_main")
	local reg = cm and cm.callback_registered and cm.callback_registered(USE_CALLBACK, old)
	if reg == false then return end -- the stock callback is not registered: nothing to guard
	if not use_guard then
		use_guard = function(obj, ...)
			if is_player() then
				local c = checkpoints()
				local sec = section_of(obj)
				local kind = c and sec and c.item_kind(sec)
				if kind == "sleepbag" and sleepbag_branch(sec) then
					-- stock Anomaly: the engine ate the bag before this callback; it comes back, then the host takes it
					give_back(sec)
					c.request("sleepbag", GIVE_BACK_MS)
					return
				elseif kind == "pack" then
					-- the client's spawned_tents is a snapshot of the host's at his entry: the host decides what is near
					c.request("pack", 0)
					return
				end
			end
			return old(obj, ...)
		end
	end
	pcall(UnregisterScriptCallback, USE_CALLBACK, old)
	RegisterScriptCallback(USE_CALLBACK, use_guard)
end

-- Player: using a tent of mine packs it up, the one I used (its position goes with the claim; the engine packs the tent of mine
-- at that spot). A sleeping bag is used to sleep.
local function on_physic_use(obj, who)
	if not is_player() or obj == nil then return end
	local c = checkpoints()
	if not c then return end
	if who ~= nil then -- the use of another player is not mine to answer
		local ok_who, wid = pcall(function() return who:id() end)
		local actor = db.actor
		if ok_who and actor and wid ~= actor:id() then return end
	end
	local ok, sec, id = pcall(function() return obj:section(), obj:id() end)
	if not ok or c.object_kind(sec) ~= "tent" then return end
	if id ~= nil and c.is_mine_tent(id, obj) then
		local pos = obj:position()
		return c.request("pack", 0, { x = pos.x, y = pos.y, z = pos.z }) == true
	end
end

-- coop_objects.cpp client_intercept_use (live 2026-10-25): a player's F on a tent stays on his machine - a Use sent to the
-- host never reached on_physic_use here. True when it asked the host to pack his tent up.
function use_tent(obj)
	if obj == nil then return false end
	return on_physic_use(obj, nil) == true
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- World server: tents the engine put up for players
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
local function register_owned(id)
	local c = checkpoints()
	local se = alife_object(id)
	local kind = se and c and c.object_kind(se:section_name())
	if not kind then return false end
	local t = spawned(kind == "sleepbag" and "get_spawned_sleepbags" or "get_spawned_tents")
	if not t then return false end
	t[id] = true
	return true
end

-- coop_tent_placed(tent, character): the engine put a tent / sleeping bag up for a player (the host player's too).
local function on_tent_placed(tent, character)
	if not is_world_server() or type(tent) ~= "number" then return end
	if register_owned(tent) then stats.registered = stats.registered + 1 end
end

-- The callback queue is lossy: for every tent and sleeping bag of the world the engine knows an owner of, make sure the
-- stock lists have it. Once per world, world server only.
local function reconcile()
	if not is_world_server() then return end
	local cp = api and api.checkpoint
	local c = checkpoints()
	if not (cp and cp.tent_owner and c) then return end
	local sim = alife and alife()
	if not (sim and sim.iterate_objects) then return end
	local tents, bags = spawned("get_spawned_tents"), spawned("get_spawned_sleepbags")
	if not (tents and bags) then return end
	local found = 0
	local ok, err = pcall(sim.iterate_objects, sim, function(se)
		local kind = c.object_kind(se:section_name())
		if kind then
			local t = kind == "sleepbag" and bags or tents
			local id = se.id
			if t[id] == nil and cp.tent_owner(id) ~= nil then
				t[id] = true
				found = found + 1
			end
		end
		return false
	end)
	if not ok then log("! looking through the world for tents failed: %s", tostring(err)) end
	stats.reconciled = stats.reconciled + found
	if found > 0 then log("%d tent(s) / sleeping bag(s) of players added to the stock lists", found) end
end

local install -- below

local function on_first_update()
	-- an entry point that a mod replaced after our on_game_start is wrapped again (review M-3)
	local ok, err = pcall(install)
	if not ok then log("! install failed: %s", tostring(err)) end
	ok, err = pcall(reconcile)
	if not ok then log("! reconcile failed: %s", tostring(err)) end
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- item_tent.get_nearby_tent over the whole list (review I-2)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- handled, value. Not handled (false): no tent of the list is online, or the arguments are not the stock ones - the stock
-- function (or the mod's) answers.
local function pick_tent(dist, result)
	if type(dist) ~= "number" then return false end
	local c = checkpoints()
	local actor = db.actor
	local tents = spawned("get_spawned_tents")
	if not (c and actor and tents) then return false end
	local ids = {}
	for id, v in pairs(tents) do
		if v == true then ids[id] = true end
	end
	local player = is_player()
	if player then
		for id in pairs(c.my_objects()) do ids[id] = true end -- his own tents, though the host's snapshot has not got them
	end
	local cp = api and api.checkpoint
	-- the host player's process holds the world's book of owners: his own tents of an older world are his too (tent_owner)
	local world = player and is_world_server() and cp and cp.tent_owner
	local here = actor:position()
	local seen = false
	local best_id, best_rank, best_dist = nil, nil, nil
	for id in pairs(ids) do
		local obj = level.object_by_id(id)
		if obj and c.object_kind(obj:section()) == "tent" then
			seen = true
			local d = obj:position():distance_to(here)
			if d < dist then
				local rank
				if player then
					rank = (c.is_mine_tent(id, obj) or (world and cp.tent_owner(id) == 0)) and 1 or 3
				else
					local owner = cp and cp.tent_owner and cp.tent_owner(id)
					rank = owner == 0 and 1 or (owner == nil and 2 or 3) -- the host's claimed tent, an unclaimed one, a client's
				end
				if best_id == nil or rank < best_rank or (rank == best_rank and d < best_dist) then
					best_id, best_rank, best_dist = id, rank, d
				end
			end
		end
	end
	if not seen then return false end
	if best_id == nil then return true, false end
	if result == true then return true, best_id end
	return true, true
end

local function nearby_tent_maker()
	return function(orig)
		return function(dist, result, ...)
			if in_session() then
				local ok, handled, value = pcall(pick_tent, dist, result)
				if ok and handled then return value end
			end
			return orig(dist, result, ...)
		end
	end
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Wrappers: name -> make(orig, mod) -> wrapper
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
local function use_functor_maker()
	return function(orig)
		return function(obj, ...)
			local c = checkpoints()
			if obj ~= nil and c and is_player() then return client_item(c, obj, orig, ...) end
			return orig(obj, ...)
		end
	end
end

local function timer_functor_maker(tent_func)
	return function(orig)
		return function(...)
			if is_player() then
				-- use_placeable = false: the stock gives the item back to the actor (a parent the host accepts), nothing is put up
				local c = checkpoints()
				if tent_func and c and not c.placeable("tent") then return orig(...) end
				return -- queued by a mod: it would index the nil of alife_create
			end
			return orig(...)
		end
	end
end

local MAKERS = {
	{ "func_use_tent", use_functor_maker() },
	{ "func_use_bag", use_functor_maker() },
	{ "itm_tent_func", timer_functor_maker(true) },
	{ "itm_tent_bag_func", timer_functor_maker(false) },
	{ "get_nearby_tent", nearby_tent_maker() },
	{ "start_timer", function(orig)
		return function(obj, ...)
			if is_player() then
				local c = checkpoints()
				local sec = section_of(obj)
				if c and sec == "itm_tent" and c.placeable("tent") then
					-- reached from the use callback: the engine ate the tent. It comes back, then the host takes it
					give_back(sec)
					c.request("tent", math.max(animation_ms(), GIVE_BACK_MS))
					return
				elseif c and sec == "itm_tent_bag" then
					c.request("pack", 0)
					return
				end
			end
			return orig(obj, ...)
		end
	end },
	{ "use_compression_bag", function(orig)
		return function(obj, dist, ...)
			if is_player() then
				local c = checkpoints()
				if c and obj ~= nil then c.request("pack", 0) end
				return
			end
			return orig(obj, dist, ...)
		end
	end },
	{ "on_game_start", function(orig)
		return function(...)
			orig(...)
			local ok, err = pcall(swap_use_callback)
			if not ok then log("! use callback swap failed: %s", tostring(err)) end
		end
	end },
}

local wrappers = {} -- entry name -> the wrapper this script put in the module table

install = function()
	if not api then return end
	local ok, mod = pcall(function() return rawget(_G, "item_tent") or _G.item_tent end) -- loads the stock script if needed
	if not (ok and type(mod) == "table") then return end
	for _, entry in ipairs(MAKERS) do
		local name, make = entry[1], entry[2]
		local cur = mod[name]
		-- A mod that overwrote the function after us is wrapped again (the adapter must not go silent).
		if type(cur) == "function" and cur ~= wrappers[name] then
			if stock_use == nil and (name == "func_use_tent" or name == "func_use_bag") then
				stock_use = upvalue(cur, "actor_on_item_use") -- the file local both functors call
			end
			local wrapper = make(cur, mod)
			if type(wrapper) == "function" then
				mod[name] = wrapper
				wrappers[name] = wrapper
			end
		end
	end
	if stock_use == nil then
		log("! the stock use callback of item_tent was not found: the sleeping bag branch stays unguarded")
	end
end

-- on_game_start must not throw: axr_main runs every script's on_game_start in one unprotected loop, and an
-- error here would skip all the scripts after this one, single player included.
function on_game_start()
	local ok, err = pcall(install)
	if not ok then log("! install failed: %s", tostring(err)) end
	-- item_tent.on_game_start may have run already (its callback is registered): swap now, otherwise its wrapper does it.
	local cm = rawget(_G, "coop_main")
	if stock_use and cm and cm.callback_registered and cm.callback_registered(USE_CALLBACK, stock_use) == true then
		local ok_swap, err_swap = pcall(swap_use_callback)
		if not ok_swap then log("! use callback swap failed: %s", tostring(err_swap)) end
	end
	if not api then return end
	local ok_reg, err_reg = pcall(function()
		AddScriptCallback("coop_tent_placed") -- fired by the engine on the host (coop_checkpoint_sources.cpp)
		RegisterScriptCallback("coop_tent_placed", on_tent_placed)
		RegisterScriptCallback("physic_object_on_use_callback", on_physic_use)
		RegisterScriptCallback("actor_on_first_update", on_first_update)
	end)
	if not ok_reg then log("! registering the callbacks failed: %s", tostring(err_reg)) end
end

-- Load time (before any on_game_start): the wrappers are in place before anybody looks the functions up.
do
	local ok, err = pcall(install)
	if not ok then printf("[coop-tent-guard] ! install at load failed: %s", tostring(err)) end
end
